From 0414e0a0bfbf7445a8dbabe591f567afbceb1cd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:16:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] macos-arm64: dynamic objects in the ray-traced geometry

Two-level acceleration structure: the static world (brushes + static props)
plus per-frame instances. Rigid meshes (physics props, doors, brush
entities) carry a prebuilt BVH and are instanced with the entity
transform; skinned models (NPCs, ragdolls) are skinned on the GPU from the
client's bone matrices into a per-object world-space copy that is refitted
each frame. The temporal pass clips history against the 3x3 neighbourhood
so occlusion from moving objects does not trail. Bounded GPU wait: a hang or
fault disables the layer instead of freezing the game.

rt_dynamic 0/1/2 (none / rigid only / rigid + skinned), rt_dynamic_range,
rt_list_dynamic.
